<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mir Mustafa Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Mustafa Khan was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a>, on the south-western coast of the Caspian, from 1786 until his death in 1814. Threatened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, he sought Russian protection and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1804-1813">Russo-Persian War</a> of 1804–1813. Russian troops stormed his capital Lankaran in January 1813, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-gulistan">Treaty of Gulistan</a> that year placed the khanate under Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p></div>
